{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nA read-based documentation audit (independently verified twice: once by the auditing agent,\nonce by the operator) found one consistent defect class across ~143k LOC: comments/docstrings\nthat were true when written and are now false — costly for LLM agents, which treat a comment as\nauthoritative and burn context chasing a dangling pointer.\n\nScoped to 9 verified sites + a read-only census of a 10th excluded family (\"Parser of record\").\n**Behaviour-preserving only**: comment/docstring corrections, 2 same-file statement moves, 1\ndead-assignment deletion, 1 new self-checking test. No control-flow changes. Re-verify every\nsite against current `origin/main` before editing (audit base was 2e28d817a7e); skip+report any\nsite that no longer matches.\n\n## Sites\n\n1. `src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py` ~12-30 + constant block: wrongly claims\n   `_STEP_VERIFY`/`_STEP_DECIDE`/`_LLM_STEP_KINDS` mirror `gate_dispatch.py` (which defines none\n   of them). Real home: `src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py` (L20/21/70). 3rd copy\n   of `_LLM_STEP_KINDS` at `runs.py:393` w/ differently-worded comment. Fix: correct both\n   comments to name `plan_review_recovery` as canonical, note the `runs.py` copy, preserve the\n   stated reason for duplication (finalize.py stays a leaf, no back-import). Add a plain test\n   (no new fixture/helper) asserting the 3-way constant equality, in the existing natural test\n   home if one exists.\n\n2. `src/rebar/reducer/_api.py` ~21-23 (`_NON_GRAPH_ARTIFACT_TYPES` has 3 members; comment names\n   2 — `identity` added by b665cff905d without updating prose) and ~247-255, plus 4 inherited\n   stale-2-type sites: `_api.py` ~247-255, `graph/_ready.py` ~92-94, `graph/_unblock.py`\n   ~167-170, `_io/export_ndjson.py` ~86-88. Fix: all 5 refer to the tuple by name instead of\n   enumerating members (follow `_engine_support/reads.py:421-424`'s existing correct pattern).\n   Do not change `export_ndjson` behaviour.\n\n3. `_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py`: ~65 cites a nonexistent\n   `_OUTBOUND_UPDATE_ALLOWLIST` (sole repo occurrence) — restate accurately or delete. ~415\n   claims `_index_existing_links` is \"duplicated\" from `apply_outbound` but only 1 definition\n   exists (~412) — delete false claim. Also independently check 2 unverified audit flags in this\n   package: `outbound_pass.py:282-284` and `applier.py:100,111-118,120`; fix if dangling, report\n   if sound.\n\n4. `llm/review_kernel/decide.py` ~681-684: `_sev = severity_label(imp)` falsely justified as\n   keeping `severity_label` \"exercised/live\" (it's exported + independently tested; `_sev` is\n   never read). Delete statement + comment. File at 782/800 LOC — net change must be negative.\n\n5. `llm/workflow/interpreter.py` ~252-259: `_commit_state` docstring falsely claims it's the\n   sole chokepoint for all writes (re-verified: multiple write sites bypass it). Re-census writes\n   against current source, correct the docstring to claim only what's verified — no guessing at\n   an unverified mechanism.\n\n6. `llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py`: `tests/unit/test_step_failures.py` ~241-255 slices this\n   module's raw source between `def _run_code_review_gate` and `def _consumed_diagnostic` —\n   making their existence/order load-bearing, invisible to rename tools. Add a short comment at\n   both ends (gate_dispatch.py, matching its existing load-bearing-note style ~34-40; and the\n   test) naming the coupling. File at 777/800 LOC — net change must be neutral or negative.\n\n7. `_engine_support/next_batch.py`: (a) move the `_blocked_ids` binding (~244) + comment above\n   the parent-story gate helpers that read it (~229); verify `open_blockers_by_ticket` isn't\n   bound later than the new spot. (b) `files_read` (`__slots__` ~61, init `set()` ~77) is never\n   assigned anywhere; emitted under a different name `files_likely_read` (~345) — a published\n   schema field, do not remove. Add a comment at the init explaining retained-for-compat,\n   matching the `skipped_needs_planning` note ~160 lines below, mentioning the rename.\n\n8. `_commands/fsck_recover.py`: `_read_or` called ~214-215, defined last in file (~330,\n   module-level, resolves fine). Move the definition above its first caller.\n\n9. `llm/plan_review/floors.py`: has 2 appliers of the same drop-a-finding algorithm as\n   `_recompute_verdict_after_drop` (`drift_floor.py:200`, called from 3 sites incl. `xcheck.py`\n   which explains why) but calls it from neither and never explains why. Determine if the\n   omission is correct; if so add a one-line note. If NOT correct, that's a behavioural bug, OUT\n   OF SCOPE — report separately, do not fix.\n\n10. (Read-only, do not edit) \"Parser of record\": ~14-21 modules carry this comment above a\n    discarded argparse factory. Pin the exact file count+line numbers, used-vs-discarded per\n    site, and resolve the audit-vs-recount discrepancy (21/15 vs 14).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Every site re-verified against current origin/main before editing; mismatches are skipped+reported.\n- Site 1 ships a new plain test (no new helper/fixture) for the 3-way constant mirror.\n- Sites 2-9: comment/docstring-only + the 2 described moves + the 1 dead-statement delete; no\n  control-flow changes.\n- `decide.py`, `gate_dispatch.py` line counts net-neutral or lower.\n- No new config key/env var/feature flag/CI gate/lock/autouse fixture/test helper (mechanism-delta ratchet clean).\n- `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` passes, no new/increased entries.\n- `make verify` passes from a fresh worktree, worktree venv first on PATH.\n- Item 10 census reported, no edits to those files.\n- Item 3's 2 unverified cross-refs independently checked, verdict reported.\n- Item 9: if the floors.py omission is a real bug, report separately, do not fix.\n- Pushed via `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`, not submitted.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793825064046036737,"uuid":"6bcb06fd-cfb2-4067-b01c-1d8158db2d73"}